>
  <p>
    Rolex service is as much about judgment as torque specs: knowing when a dial should stay untouched, when
    a bezel insert is part of the story, and when water resistance testing is non-negotiable after a
    crystal job. Shelton Watch Services approaches Rolex work with collector-aware conservatism — and modern
    owners get plain-language options, not a black box.
  </p>
  <h2>What we evaluate first</h2>
  <p>
    Timing traces, amplitude hints, crown feel, date change behavior, and any evidence of moisture or
    magnetism. The goal is to separate “running acceptably” from “running sustainably” — especially on
    bracelets that see desk-dive duty across the Lehigh Valley.
  </p>
  <h2>Services &amp; typical starting points</h2>
  <p>
    Battery-free models receive mechanical servicing: disassembly, cleaning, lubrication, reassembly,
    regulation, and testing. Quartz Rolex models are less common but supported when they appear. Cosmetic
    refinishing is optional and discussed before any abrasive work begins.
  </p>
</ServiceBrandPage>
